    "body": "## Goal\nDetermine which Chinese-origin automotive technology, if any, can lawfully be used in a U.S. HAVEN production vehicle.\n\n### Required work\n- [ ] Engage U.S. trade and vehicle cybersecurity counsel before Chinese ADAS/AI/telematics software or platform procurement (founder approval required for spend).\n- [ ] Review BIS January 2025 connected vehicle final rule at https://media.bis.gov/connected-vehicles and 15 CFR Part 791.\n- [ ] Map MY2027 covered software and MY2030 VCS hardware restrictions; analyze supplier ownership/control and development origin.\n- [ ] Identify exempt / permitted products and applicable authorizations; do **not** treat all China-manufactured commodities as banned.\n- [ ] Compare US/EU/Japan/Korea-certified independent suppliers capable of comparable cabin AI, ADAS and core controller capabilities.\n- [ ] Require audit trail, independent safety case, software provenance, cybersecurity update rights, warranty, source/toolchain access and field service.\n- [ ] Record legal open questions, costs and decision owners privately.\n\n### Acceptance\nQualified counsel's dated sourcing framework and product-module supplier eligibility matrix; status remains OPEN until review.\n\n**No importation or contracts authorized.**",
